+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+Send `{ "tickets": [...] }`, with zero to 5000 items using the same fields and validation as `POST /tickets`.
+All items are checked before any change. An invalid item returns 400 in the normal error envelope; its message
+names `tickets[index]` for the first invalid item, counting from zero. No ticket, id, audit entry or notification
+is consumed on validation failure.
+
+Success returns 201 with `{ "created": 2, "ids": ["T-0001", "T-0002"] }`, in input order. Each ticket has
+its usual creation audit entry (including `X-Actor`) and requester notification in the outbox. The whole import
+is saved once. An empty array returns `{ "created": 0, "ids": [] }`.
+
+This endpoint accepts up to the larger of 16 MiB and `MAX_BODY_BYTES`, allowing full batches without changing
+the ordinary endpoints' configured body limit.
+
 ### List tickets: `GET /tickets`
 
